  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first experiment is to establish a strong upper-bound baseline using the most powerful components across all design dimensions: multimodal model setting (the core hypothesis of the study), multiprofile (richest cellular context), scgpt (pretrained foundation-model RNA encoder), imagenet_vit_l (largest image encoder), transformer aggregation (most expressive token-level aggregation), and weighted fusion (learned modality weighting). This configuration tests whether the full-power multimodal pipeline can achieve high validation accuracy, giving a reference point against which all subsequent ablations (simpler encoders, different aggregation, singleprofile, unimodal baselines) can be compared. If it performs well, the remaining 9 experiments can systematically ablate components to identify what drives performance. If it underperforms, it signals that complexity is hurting and I should pivot toward simpler or unimodal alternatives. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the tight 10-experiment budget."
}

